-- @@section 372
-- 372 Explanation: "When a female below 21 years of age is sold, let for hire,
-- or otherwise disposed of to a prostitute or to any person who keeps or
-- manages a brothel, the person so disposing of such female shall, until the
-- contrary is proved, be presumed to have disposed of her with the intent that
-- she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution."
-- 373 Explanation is the mirror: a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a
-- female below 21.
DECLARE `Presumption of intent to use for prostitution` IS ONE OF
    `presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had the intent that she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution`
    `not covered by this Explanation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 Explanation (src:8080-8083)
@export What the Explanation to section 372 of the Penal Code 1871 presumes: that a person who disposes of a female below 21 years of age to a prostitute or a brothel-keeper intended her to be used for prostitution, until the contrary is proved
GIVEN `the person disposed of is a female below 21 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who was sold, let for hire or otherwise disposed of a female below 21 years of age?
      `the disposal is to a prostitute or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was she disposed of to a prostitute, or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel?
GIVETH A `Presumption of intent to use for prostitution`
`s 372 Explanation the intent that she shall be used for prostitution` MEANS
    IF `the person disposed of is a female below 21 years of age` AND `the disposal is to a prostitute or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel`
    THEN `presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had the intent that she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution`
    ELSE `not covered by this Explanation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Explanation presumes the intent only for a female below 21 disposed of to a prostitute or brothel-keeper; it does not say that the intent is not to be found in any other case

-- @@section 373
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 Explanation (src:8094-8097)
@export What the Explanation to section 373 of the Penal Code 1871 presumes: that a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a female below 21 years of age intended her to be used for prostitution, until the contrary is proved
GIVEN `the person who obtains possession is a prostitute or a person keeping or managing a brothel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who bought, hired or otherwise obtained possession a prostitute, or a person who keeps or manages a brothel?
      `the person obtained is a female below 21 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person obtained a female below 21 years of age?
GIVETH A `Presumption of intent to use for prostitution`
`s 373 Explanation the intent that she shall be used for prostitution` MEANS
    IF `the person who obtains possession is a prostitute or a person keeping or managing a brothel` AND `the person obtained is a female below 21 years of age`
    THEN `presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had the intent that she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution`
    ELSE `not covered by this Explanation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Explanation presumes the intent only for a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a female below 21; it does not say that the intent is not to be found in any other case

-- @@section 376B
-- 376B(4): "sexual services" means any sexual services involving (a)-(c)
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(4) (src:8373-8383)
@export Whether services are "sexual services" within section 376B(4) of the Penal Code 1871: services involving sexual penetration of the vagina or anus by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else, penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth by a man's penis, or touching which is sexual
GIVEN `the services involve sexual penetration of the vagina or anus of a person by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the services involve that?
      `the services involve penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth of a person by a man's penis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the services involve that?
      `the services involve touching which is sexual of another person or of himself or herself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the services involve touching which is sexual? "Sexual" is read with `s 377C(2) the touching is sexual`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376B(4) the services are sexual services` MEANS
    IF `the services involve sexual penetration of the vagina or anus of a person by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else`
        OR `the services involve penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth of a person by a man's penis`
        OR `the services involve touching which is sexual of another person or of himself or herself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"sexual services\" means any sexual services involving ..." (a closed list)

-- @@section 376D
-- 376D(2): the publication of information means publication by any means
DECLARE `Form of communication` IS ONE OF
    written
    electronic
    `some other form of communication`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D(2) (src:8431-8435)
@export Whether a form of communication is "publication of information" within section 376D(2) of the Penal Code 1871: "publication of information by any means, whether by written, electronic, or other form of communication"
GIVEN form IS A `Form of communication` @desc The form in which the information was published
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376D(2) the means of publication` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN written THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN electronic THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other form of communication` THEN JUST TRUE

-- @@section 376E
-- 376E(2)(a), 376EA(2)(a): the relevant offences of the Penal Code (a closed list, "means")
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(2)(a) (src:8488-8490)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the offences relevant under section 376E(2)` MEANS
    LIST "354", "354A", "355", "372", "373", "373A", "375", "376", "376A", "376B", "376C",
         "376EB", "376ED", "376F", "376H",
         "377(1)(e)", "377(1)(f)", "377(1)(g)", "377(1)(h)", "377B(3)",
         "377BA", "377BB", "377BF", "377BG", "377BH"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(2) (src:8486-8497)
@export Whether an offence is a "relevant offence" within section 376E(2) of the Penal Code 1871: an offence under the listed sections of the Code, section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993, or section 140(1) of the Women's Charter 1961
GIVEN offence IS A STRING @desc The offence A intends to commit, cited as the section of the Penal Code 1871 ("375", "377(1)(e)"), or as "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8" or "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)"; any other text is another offence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376E(2) the offence is a relevant offence` MEANS
    IF elem offence (`the offences relevant under section 376E(2)`)
        OR offence EQUALS "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8"
        OR offence EQUALS "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"relevant offence\" means an offence under — ..." (a closed list)

-- @@section 376EA
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(2)(a) (src:8574-8576)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the offences relevant under section 376EA(2)` MEANS
    LIST "354", "354A", "355", "372", "373", "373A", "375", "376", "376AA", "376B", "376C",
         "376EC", "376EE", "376F", "376G", "376H",
         "377(1)(e)", "377(1)(f)", "377(1)(g)", "377(1)(h)", "377B(3)",
         "377BA", "377BB", "377BF", "377BL"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(2) (src:8572-8586)
@export Whether an offence is a "relevant offence" within section 376EA(2) of the Penal Code 1871: an offence under the listed sections of the Code, section 140(1) of the Women's Charter 1961, or section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993
GIVEN offence IS A STRING @desc The offence A intends to commit, cited as the section of the Penal Code 1871 ("375", "377(1)(e)"), or as "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)" or "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8"; any other text is another offence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376EA(2) the offence is a relevant offence` MEANS
    IF elem offence (`the offences relevant under section 376EA(2)`)
        OR offence EQUALS "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)"
        OR offence EQUALS "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"relevant offence\" means an offence under — ..." (a closed list)

-- @@section 376F
-- 376F(5): "mental disability" means ...
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(5) (src:8843-8846)
@export Whether an impairment is a "mental disability" within section 376F(5) of the Penal Code 1871: an impairment of or disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain, resulting from any disability or disorder of the mind or brain, which impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching
GIVEN `there is an impairment of or a disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain resulting from a disability or disorder of the mind or brain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such an impairment or disturbance?
      `it impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it impair that ability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376F(5) the impairment is a mental disability` MEANS
    IF `there is an impairment of or a disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain resulting from a disability or disorder of the mind or brain`
        AND `it impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"mental disability\" means an impairment of or a disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain ... which impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching"

-- @@section 376G
-- 376G(2): "B is a close family relative of A if B is A's grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling, parent or grandparent"
DECLARE `Relation of B to A` IS ONE OF
    grandchild
    child
    sibling
    `half-sibling`
    parent
    grandparent
    `another relation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(2) (src:8876-8878)
@export Whether B is a "close family relative" of A within section 376G(2) of the Penal Code 1871, by B's relation to A (whether or not the relationship is traced through lawful wedlock)
GIVEN relation IS A `Relation of B to A` @desc B's relation to A
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376G(2) B is a close family relative of A` MEANS
    CONSIDER relation
    WHEN grandchild THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN child THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN sibling THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `half-sibling` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN parent THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN grandparent THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another relation` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "B is a close family relative of A if B is A's grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling, parent or grandparent" (an "if" read as closing the list: marginal reading a)

-- 376G(4): the act that "would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1)"
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(4) (src:8887-8889)
@export Whether an act of penetration is one that would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1) of the Penal Code 1871, so that section 376G does not apply to it
GIVEN n IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The facts of the same act of penetration, read under sections 375, 376 and 376AA
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an act of penetration excluded from section 376G by section 376G(4)` n IF
        (        n's `the accused is a man`
            AND  n's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
            AND  n's `the victim is a woman`
            AND  `without consent within section 375(a)` n )
    OR  (        n's `the accused is a man`
            AND  n's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`
            AND  `without consent within section 375(a)` n )
    OR  `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` n
    OR  `commits exploitative sexual penetration of a minor within section 376AA(1)` n

-- 376G(5) and 376A(1B): consent is immaterial ("To avoid doubt")
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(5) (src:8894-8899)
@export Whether, under section 376G(5)(a) of the Penal Code 1871, the prosecution must prove that B did consent to the act of penetration: it need not
GIVEN `B did consent to the act of penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B consent? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376G(5)(a) the prosecution must prove that B did consent` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove that B did consent to the act of penetration"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(5) (src:8894-8899)
@export Whether, under section 376G(5)(b) of the Penal Code 1871, it is a defence that B did consent to the act of penetration: it is not
GIVEN `B did consent to the act of penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B consent? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376G(5)(b) B's consent is a defence` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not a defence that B did consent to that act"

-- @@section 376H
-- 376H(3): rules of reading
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(3)(a) (src:8962-8963)
@export Whether a person makes a "false representation" within section 376H(3)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: the representation is untrue or misleading, and the person knows that it is, or might be
GIVEN `the representation is untrue or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the representation untrue or misleading?
      `the person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who made it know that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376H(3)(a) the representation is false` MEANS
    IF `the representation is untrue or misleading` AND `the person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person makes a false representation if it is untrue or misleading, and that person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

DECLARE `Form of a representation` IS ONE OF
    express
    implied
    `some other form of representation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(3)(b) (src:8965-8965)
@export Whether a representation of the given form is a representation within section 376H(3)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: "a representation may be express or implied"
GIVEN form IS A `Form of a representation` @desc The form in which the representation was made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376H(3)(b) the representation is express or implied` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN express THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN implied THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other form of representation` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a representation may be express or implied" says two forms count; it does not say that a representation in no such form is not one

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(3)(c) (src:8968-8974)
@export Whether a thing is a "sexually protective measure" within section 376H(3)(c) of the Penal Code 1871: where B is female, a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy or sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse; where B is male, one to prevent sexually transmitted diseases
GIVEN `B is female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B female?
      `B is male` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B male?
      `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy as a result of sexual intercourse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy as a result of sexual intercourse?
      `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376H(3)(c) the thing is a sexually protective measure` MEANS
    IF (        `B is female`
           AND  (     `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy as a result of sexual intercourse`
                  OR  `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse` ) )
       OR  (    `B is male`
           AND  `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse` )
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a \"sexually protective measure\" means ..." (a closed definition)
